{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 23:14:24", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-478dffcf-bd6d-4bef-a783-0dc5d88505b6', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "API Cost Optimization - Local Claude & OpenAI Integration"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01M3MJanBt77znC37herJ2ur', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01M3MJanBt77znC37herJ2ur', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# API Cost Optimization Research & Implementation Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name**: API Cost Optimization - Local Claude & OpenAI Integration  \\n**Objective**: Research and implement support for delegating tasks to local Claude instance and OpenAI API to reduce Anthropic API costs while maintaining quality\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nThe current Ensemble system exclusively uses Anthropic\'s Claude API for all agent operations, resulting in significant API costs. The user wants to:\\n\\n1. **Cost Reduction**: Find ways to reduce API expenses by leveraging alternative model providers\\n2. **Local Claude Integration**: Investigate using local Claude instances when available and suitable for autonomous tasks\\n3. **OpenAI API Support**: Add OpenAI API as an alternative provider for appropriate tasks\\n4. **Quality Maintenance**: Ensure delegation decisions maintain output quality and system functionality\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Research & Documentation (Phase 1)\\n\\n**Research Document Deliverable**:\\n- Analyze current Anthropic API usage patterns across all agent types\\n- Document which agent tasks can operate autonomously (no user interaction needed)\\n- Research local Claude deployment options (ollama, local API servers, etc.)\\n- Evaluate OpenAI model capabilities vs current Claude usage\\n- Define cost comparison matrix between providers\\n- Create decision framework for model selection based on task complexity and autonomy level\\n- Document implementation approach and architecture changes needed\\n\\n**Agent Documentation Audit**:\\n- Review all 40+ agent definitions to identify:\\n  - Which agents perform fully autonomous tasks\\n  - Current model requirements and complexity ratings\\n  - Tasks suitable for local/cheaper models\\n  - Critical tasks requiring premium models\\n\\n### 2. OpenAI API Integration (Phase 2)\\n\\n**Technical Implementation**:\\n- Extend `runtime.py` to support OpenAI API alongside Anthropic\\n- Modify `model_selector.py` to include OpenAI models in selection logic\\n- Update `cost_calculator.py` for OpenAI pricing\\n- Add OpenAI configuration to environment management\\n- Implement fallback mechanisms (OpenAI \\u2192 Anthropic \\u2192 Local Claude)\\n\\n**Model Mapping**:\\n- Map agent complexity levels to appropriate OpenAI models (GPT-4, GPT-3.5-turbo, etc.)\\n- Update budget tier system to include OpenAI options\\n- Implement dynamic model selection based on task autonomy and complexity\\n\\n### 3. Local Claude Integration (Phase 3)\\n\\n**Local Provider Detection**:\\n- Auto-detect available local Claude instances (check common ports, endpoints)\\n- Implement health checks for local providers\\n- Create configuration system for local endpoint URLs\\n\\n**Task Delegation Logic**:\\n- Define criteria for local delegation:\\n  - Task can complete autonomously (no user input required)\\n  - Task complexity is low-to-medium\\n  - Local instance is healthy and responsive\\n- Implement intelligent routing: Local \\u2192 OpenAI \\u2192 Anthropic\\n\\n### 4. Cost Optimization Framework\\n\\n**Smart Model Selection**:\\n- Dynamic model selection based on:\\n  - Task autonomy level (fully autonomous vs requires user input)\\n  - Agent type and complexity rating\\n  - Available provider health status\\n  - Cost optimization goals vs quality requirements\\n- Implement cost tracking and reporting per provider\\n\\n**Quality Safeguards**:\\n- Automatic quality assessment of local/cheaper model outputs\\n- Fallback to premium models if quality metrics fail\\n- A/B testing framework to validate cost optimizations maintain quality\\n\\n## Technical Architecture\\n\\n### Current State Analysis\\n- **Runtime System**: `/src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` - Anthropic-only implementation\\n- **Model Selection**: `/src/runtime/agents/model_selector.py` - Claude model selection only\\n- **Cost Tracking**: `/src/runtime/agents/cost_calculator.py` - Anthropic pricing only\\n- **Agent Definitions**: 40+ agents with varying complexity and autonomy levels\\n\\n### Proposed Architecture\\n```\\nCost Optimization Layer\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Provider Manager\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AnthropicProvider (existing)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 OpenAIProvider (new)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 LocalClaudeProvider (new)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Smart Router\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Task Analyzer (autonomy detection)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Provider Selector (cost/quality optimization)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Fallback Handler\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Quality Monitor\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Output Validator\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Cost Tracker (multi-provider)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Performance Reporter\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n1. **Provider Support**: System supports Anthropic, OpenAI, and local Claude providers\\n2. **Automatic Routing**: Tasks automatically route to most cost-effective suitable provider\\n3. **Quality Maintenance**: Output quality metrics remain within 95% of baseline\\n4. **Cost Reduction**: Achieve 30-50% cost reduction on autonomous tasks\\n5. **Fallback Reliability**: Seamless fallback when preferred providers fail\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n1. **Backward Compatibility**: Existing agent definitions work without modification\\n2. **Configuration Flexibility**: Easy provider enablement/disablement via config\\n3. **Monitoring**: Comprehensive cost and quality tracking across providers\\n4. **Documentation**: Clear setup instructions for each provider type\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- **Training Custom Models**: Focus on existing model APIs only\\n- **Agent Definition Modifications**: Avoid changing agent behaviors/capabilities\\n- **UI Changes**: Backend optimization only (UI changes come later)\\n- **Real-time Model Switching**: Single model per agent execution (no mid-task switching)\\n\\n## Constraints & Assumptions\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing agent hierarchy and spawn permissions\\n- Cannot break existing test suite\\n- Must preserve current debugging and metrics capabilities\\n\\n### Business Constraints\\n- No breaking changes to user-facing functionality\\n- Implementation must be reversible (can disable new providers)\\n- Quality cannot degrade below acceptable thresholds\\n\\n### Assumptions\\n- User has or can obtain OpenAI API credentials\\n- Local Claude instances (when available) have compatible APIs\\n- Cost savings justify implementation complexity\\n- Autonomous tasks can be reliably identified programmatically\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n### Research First Strategy\\n1. **Phase 1**: Comprehensive research document with findings and recommendations\\n2. **Phase 2**: OpenAI integration as proof-of-concept for multi-provider approach\\n3. **Phase 3**: Local Claude integration based on research findings\\n4. **Phase 4**: Optimization and quality validation\\n\\n### Risk Mitigation\\n- Implement feature flags for gradual rollout\\n- Maintain detailed logging for debugging provider issues\\n- Create rollback procedures for each integration phase\\n- Establish quality baselines before implementing changes\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n### Research Phase\\n- **Research Document**: Comprehensive analysis and implementation recommendations\\n- **Cost Analysis**: Provider comparison matrix with pricing projections\\n- **Agent Audit**: Documentation of autonomy levels and provider suitability per agent\\n- **Architecture Design**: Detailed technical design for multi-provider support\\n\\n### Implementation Phase\\n- **Provider Integration**: Working OpenAI and local Claude provider support\\n- **Smart Router**: Intelligent task-to-provider mapping system\\n- **Monitoring System**: Cost and quality tracking across providers\\n- **Documentation**: Setup guides and configuration reference\\n- **Test Suite**: Comprehensive tests for multi-provider scenarios\\n\\n## Notes & Context\\n\\n- User submitted via web UI seeking cost optimization for the ensemble system\\n- Current system has 40+ specialized agents with varying complexity levels\\n- Focus on autonomous task delegation to preserve user experience\\n- OpenAI integration serves as stepping stone to broader provider ecosystem\\n- Research document should inform implementation priorities and approaches\\n\\""}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 62.9%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.8\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Focus on completing tasks successfully - your success rate needs improvement.\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively managed project completion by thoroughly reviewing the milestone status document, updating project tracking records, and creating comprehensive completion documentation. My approach focu...\n- Executed a comprehensive validation project with systematic approach, leveraging multiple agents to design, implement, and validate the A/B testing framework. Demonstrated ability to drive project fro...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'