{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 23:17:24", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-dd47fd31-b4db-4e91-adf7-1d586ba3b805', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Research & Documentation (Phase 1) - Complete comprehensive research and documentation to inform implementation strategy including current API usage analysis, agent audit, cost comparison matrix, and technical architecture design",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MVa8LnjxrwzrBW9urhj1m7', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TSpSpcCaooRDN3ZBMoZ5X8', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MVa8LnjxrwzrBW9urhj1m7', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: API Cost Optimization System\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Design Philosophy\\nA flexible, extensible multi-provider architecture that enables intelligent, cost-effective AI model routing while maintaining system reliability and output quality.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n- **Layered Architecture** with clear separation of concerns\\n- **Strategy Pattern** for provider management\\n- **Decorator/Proxy Pattern** for quality monitoring and fallback\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Provider SDKs**: \\n  - Anthropic Claude: `anthropic` \\n  - OpenAI: `openai`\\n  - Local Providers: Custom REST client\\n\\n### Key Libraries\\n- `pydantic` for configuration and validation\\n- `asyncio` for concurrent provider interactions\\n- `prometheus_client` for metrics tracking\\n- `structlog` for structured logging\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### A. Provider Management Layer\\n```\\nProviderManager\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 BaseProvider (Abstract Base Class)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AnthropicProvider\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 OpenAIProvider\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 LocalClaudeProvider\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ProviderRegistry\\n```\\n\\n#### Responsibilities:\\n- Standardized interface for different AI providers\\n- Dynamic provider registration\\n- Health check mechanisms\\n- Credential management\\n\\n### B. Smart Router\\n```\\nSmartRouter\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TaskAnalyzer\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AutonomyClassifier\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProviderSelector\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 CostOptimizer\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 QualityPredictor\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 FallbackHandler\\n```\\n\\n#### Responsibilities:\\n- Analyze task complexity and autonomy\\n- Select most appropriate provider\\n- Implement intelligent fallback logic\\n\\n### C. Quality Monitoring\\n```\\nQualityMonitor\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 OutputValidator\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ModelQualityScorer\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 CostTracker\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 PerformanceReporter\\n```\\n\\n#### Responsibilities:\\n- Validate model output quality\\n- Track per-provider performance\\n- Generate cost optimization reports\\n\\n## 4. File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 providers/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 base_provider.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 anthropic_provider.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 openai_provider.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 local_claude_provider.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 routing/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 smart_router.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 task_analyzer.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 provider_selector.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 monitoring/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 quality_monitor.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 output_validator.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 cost_tracker.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 config/\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 providers.yaml\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 cost_rules.json\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Data Flow\\n\\n```\\nTask Submission \\n  \\u2193\\nTaskAnalyzer (Complexity & Autonomy Assessment)\\n  \\u2193\\nProviderSelector (Select Optimal Provider)\\n  \\u2193\\nSelected Provider Execution\\n  \\u2193\\nQualityMonitor (Validate Output)\\n  \\u2193\\nResult Return or Fallback\\n```\\n\\n## 6. Configuration Management\\n\\n### Provider Configuration (providers.yaml)\\n```yaml\\nproviders:\\n  anthropic:\\n    default_model: claude-2\\n    priority: 1\\n  openai:\\n    default_model: gpt-4\\n    priority: 2\\n  local_claude:\\n    endpoint: http://localhost:8000\\n    priority: 3\\n```\\n\\n## 7. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Containerization\\n- Docker containers for each provider adapter\\n- Kubernetes for orchestration and scaling\\n- Helm charts for configuration management\\n\\n### CI/CD\\n- GitHub Actions for testing\\n- Automated provider health checks\\n- Feature flag support for gradual rollout\\n\\n## 8. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Test Suites\\n- Unit Tests: Provider adapters, routing logic\\n- Integration Tests: Cross-provider workflows\\n- Performance Tests: Provider latency and cost\\n- Chaos Tests: Simulate provider failures\\n\\n### Quality Metrics\\n- Output similarity across providers\\n- Latency comparisons\\n- Cost per successful task\\n- Fallback success rates\\n\\n## 9. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. Inconsistent model quality\\n2. Higher complexity\\n3. Performance overhead\\n\\n### Mitigation Strategies\\n- Comprehensive quality scoring\\n- Intelligent caching\\n- Minimal abstraction overhead\\n- Detailed performance monitoring\\n\\n## 10. Open Questions for User\\n\\n1. Specific OpenAI model preferences?\\n2. Tolerance for minor quality variations?\\n3. Acceptable fallback chain priorities?\\n\\n## 11. Future Extensibility\\n\\n- Easy addition of new providers\\n- Pluggable quality assessment algorithms\\n- Machine learning-based provider selection\\n\\n## Appendix: Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Research & Base Infrastructure\\n- Provider abstract interfaces\\n- Basic routing mechanisms\\n- Logging and metrics setup\\n\\n### Phase 2: OpenAI Integration\\n- OpenAI provider implementation\\n- Cost tracking enhancements\\n- Initial routing logic\\n\\n### Phase 3: Local Claude Support\\n- Local provider detection\\n- Health check mechanisms\\n- Fallback implementations\\n\\n## Performance Targets\\n\\n- Reduce API costs by 40%\\n- Maintain 95% output quality\\n- < 50ms additional routing overhead"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TSpSpcCaooRDN3ZBMoZ5X8', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# API Cost Optimization Research & Implementation Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name**: API Cost Optimization - Local Claude & OpenAI Integration  \\n**Objective**: Research and implement support for delegating tasks to local Claude instance and OpenAI API to reduce Anthropic API costs while maintaining quality\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nThe current Ensemble system exclusively uses Anthropic\'s Claude API for all agent operations, resulting in significant API costs. The user wants to:\\n\\n1. **Cost Reduction**: Find ways to reduce API expenses by leveraging alternative model providers\\n2. **Local Claude Integration**: Investigate using local Claude instances when available and suitable for autonomous tasks\\n3. **OpenAI API Support**: Add OpenAI API as an alternative provider for appropriate tasks\\n4. **Quality Maintenance**: Ensure delegation decisions maintain output quality and system functionality\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Research & Documentation (Phase 1)\\n\\n**Research Document Deliverable**:\\n- Analyze current Anthropic API usage patterns across all agent types\\n- Document which agent tasks can operate autonomously (no user interaction needed)\\n- Research local Claude deployment options (ollama, local API servers, etc.)\\n- Evaluate OpenAI model capabilities vs current Claude usage\\n- Define cost comparison matrix between providers\\n- Create decision framework for model selection based on task complexity and autonomy level\\n- Document implementation approach and architecture changes needed\\n\\n**Agent Documentation Audit**:\\n- Review all 40+ agent definitions to identify:\\n  - Which agents perform fully autonomous tasks\\n  - Current model requirements and complexity ratings\\n  - Tasks suitable for local/cheaper models\\n  - Critical tasks requiring premium models\\n\\n### 2. OpenAI API Integration (Phase 2)\\n\\n**Technical Implementation**:\\n- Extend `runtime.py` to support OpenAI API alongside Anthropic\\n- Modify `model_selector.py` to include OpenAI models in selection logic\\n- Update `cost_calculator.py` for OpenAI pricing\\n- Add OpenAI configuration to environment management\\n- Implement fallback mechanisms (OpenAI \\u2192 Anthropic \\u2192 Local Claude)\\n\\n**Model Mapping**:\\n- Map agent complexity levels to appropriate OpenAI models (GPT-4, GPT-3.5-turbo, etc.)\\n- Update budget tier system to include OpenAI options\\n- Implement dynamic model selection based on task autonomy and complexity\\n\\n### 3. Local Claude Integration (Phase 3)\\n\\n**Local Provider Detection**:\\n- Auto-detect available local Claude instances (check common ports, endpoints)\\n- Implement health checks for local providers\\n- Create configuration system for local endpoint URLs\\n\\n**Task Delegation Logic**:\\n- Define criteria for local delegation:\\n  - Task can complete autonomously (no user input required)\\n  - Task complexity is low-to-medium\\n  - Local instance is healthy and responsive\\n- Implement intelligent routing: Local \\u2192 OpenAI \\u2192 Anthropic\\n\\n### 4. Cost Optimization Framework\\n\\n**Smart Model Selection**:\\n- Dynamic model selection based on:\\n  - Task autonomy level (fully autonomous vs requires user input)\\n  - Agent type and complexity rating\\n  - Available provider health status\\n  - Cost optimization goals vs quality requirements\\n- Implement cost tracking and reporting per provider\\n\\n**Quality Safeguards**:\\n- Automatic quality assessment of local/cheaper model outputs\\n- Fallback to premium models if quality metrics fail\\n- A/B testing framework to validate cost optimizations maintain quality\\n\\n## Technical Architecture\\n\\n### Current State Analysis\\n- **Runtime System**: `/src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` - Anthropic-only implementation\\n- **Model Selection**: `/src/runtime/agents/model_selector.py` - Claude model selection only\\n- **Cost Tracking**: `/src/runtime/agents/cost_calculator.py` - Anthropic pricing only\\n- **Agent Definitions**: 40+ agents with varying complexity and autonomy levels\\n\\n### Proposed Architecture\\n```\\nCost Optimization Layer\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Provider Manager\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AnthropicProvider (existing)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 OpenAIProvider (new)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 LocalClaudeProvider (new)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Smart Router\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Task Analyzer (autonomy detection)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Provider Selector (cost/quality optimization)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Fallback Handler\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Quality Monitor\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Output Validator\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Cost Tracker (multi-provider)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Performance Reporter\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n1. **Provider Support**: System supports Anthropic, OpenAI, and local Claude providers\\n2. **Automatic Routing**: Tasks automatically route to most cost-effective suitable provider\\n3. **Quality Maintenance**: Output quality metrics remain within 95% of baseline\\n4. **Cost Reduction**: Achieve 30-50% cost reduction on autonomous tasks\\n5. **Fallback Reliability**: Seamless fallback when preferred providers fail\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n1. **Backward Compatibility**: Existing agent definitions work without modification\\n2. **Configuration Flexibility**: Easy provider enablement/disablement via config\\n3. **Monitoring**: Comprehensive cost and quality tracking across providers\\n4. **Documentation**: Clear setup instructions for each provider type\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- **Training Custom Models**: Focus on existing model APIs only\\n- **Agent Definition Modifications**: Avoid changing agent behaviors/capabilities\\n- **UI Changes**: Backend optimization only (UI changes come later)\\n- **Real-time Model Switching**: Single model per agent execution (no mid-task switching)\\n\\n## Constraints & Assumptions\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing agent hierarchy and spawn permissions\\n- Cannot break existing test suite\\n- Must preserve current debugging and metrics capabilities\\n\\n### Business Constraints\\n- No breaking changes to user-facing functionality\\n- Implementation must be reversible (can disable new providers)\\n- Quality cannot degrade below acceptable thresholds\\n\\n### Assumptions\\n- User has or can obtain OpenAI API credentials\\n- Local Claude instances (when available) have compatible APIs\\n- Cost savings justify implementation complexity\\n- Autonomous tasks can be reliably identified programmatically\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n### Research First Strategy\\n1. **Phase 1**: Comprehensive research document with findings and recommendations\\n2. **Phase 2**: OpenAI integration as proof-of-concept for multi-provider approach\\n3. **Phase 3**: Local Claude integration based on research findings\\n4. **Phase 4**: Optimization and quality validation\\n\\n### Risk Mitigation\\n- Implement feature flags for gradual rollout\\n- Maintain detailed logging for debugging provider issues\\n- Create rollback procedures for each integration phase\\n- Establish quality baselines before implementing changes\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n### Research Phase\\n- **Research Document**: Comprehensive analysis and implementation recommendations\\n- **Cost Analysis**: Provider comparison matrix with pricing projections\\n- **Agent Audit**: Documentation of autonomy levels and provider suitability per agent\\n- **Architecture Design**: Detailed technical design for multi-provider support\\n\\n### Implementation Phase\\n- **Provider Integration**: Working OpenAI and local Claude provider support\\n- **Smart Router**: Intelligent task-to-provider mapping system\\n- **Monitoring System**: Cost and quality tracking across providers\\n- **Documentation**: Setup guides and configuration reference\\n- **Test Suite**: Comprehensive tests for multi-provider scenarios\\n\\n## Notes & Context\\n\\n- User submitted via web UI seeking cost optimization for the ensemble system\\n- Current system has 40+ specialized agents with varying complexity levels\\n- Focus on autonomous task delegation to preserve user experience\\n- OpenAI integration serves as stepping stone to broader provider ecosystem\\n- Research document should inform implementation priorities and approaches\\n\\""}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-5-20251101', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 98.3%\n- Average iterations per task: 4.3\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
