{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 23:29:11", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-d2d7007e-583c-43e9-824f-49e163da02aa', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Milestone 1: Backend API Foundation - Create retry-failed and job cleanup API endpoints including: POST /api/agents/retry-all-failed, POST /api/agents/{agent_id}/retry-and-delete, DELETE /api/jobs/completed, GET /api/jobs/completed/stats, GET /api/system/db-stats. Modify swarm_recovery.py for retry tracking and auto-delete on second failure. Modify swarm_state.py with new delete methods.",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01QRmmf4fiyS8TKwFtu2Xa8r', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Dt8vP1trxLoudCq27i4H7c', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01QRmmf4fiyS8TKwFtu2Xa8r', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture: Agent Management & Cleanup System\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Design Philosophy\\nExtend the existing ensemble UI system with retry-and-delete functionality for failed agents, job cleanup features, and performance optimizations while maintaining backwards compatibility.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n- **Extension Architecture** - Adding to existing FastAPI backend and React frontend\\n- **Repository Pattern** - Using existing `SwarmState` for data operations\\n- **Service Pattern** - New service layer for retry and cleanup logic\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack (Existing)\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\\n- **Database**: SQLite via SwarmState\\n- **Recovery**: swarm_recovery.py (existing)\\n- **State Management**: swarm_state.py (existing)\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React\\n- **Components**: Existing RecoveryDashboard, App.jsx\\n- **Styling**: Existing CSS/component library\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### A. Backend - New/Modified Components\\n\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/agents/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 swarm_recovery.py (MODIFY)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Add: track retry attempts, auto-delete on second failure\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 swarm_state.py (MODIFY)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Add: delete_agent(), delete_session(), get_completed_sessions_stats()\\n\\u2502\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/backend/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 main.py (MODIFY)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Add: retry-all-failed, retry-and-delete, job cleanup endpoints\\n```\\n\\n### B. Frontend - New/Modified Components\\n\\n```\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 JobCleanupPanel.jsx (NEW)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 CompletedJobsList\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AgeFilterSelector\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 BulkDeleteButton\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ConfirmationModal\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 RecoveryDashboard.jsx (MODIFY)\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Add: RetryAllFailedButton\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 App.jsx (MODIFY)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Add: Route to JobCleanupPanel\\n```\\n\\n## 4. API Design\\n\\n### New Endpoints\\n\\n#### Retry Failed Agents\\n```\\nPOST /api/agents/retry-all-failed\\nResponse: { \\"queued_count\\": int, \\"agent_ids\\": list[str] }\\n\\nPOST /api/agents/{agent_id}/retry-and-delete\\nResponse: { \\"status\\": \\"queued\\" | \\"deleted\\" | \\"succeeded\\", \\"agent_id\\": str }\\n```\\n\\n#### Job Cleanup\\n```\\nGET /api/jobs/completed/stats\\nResponse: {\\n  \\"total_completed\\": int,\\n  \\"by_age\\": [\\n    { \\"age_days\\": \\"0-7\\", \\"count\\": int, \\"size_mb\\": float },\\n    { \\"age_days\\": \\"7-30\\", \\"count\\": int, \\"size_mb\\": float },\\n    { \\"age_days\\": \\"30+\\", \\"count\\": int, \\"size_mb\\": float }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\nDELETE /api/jobs/completed\\nQuery Params: older_than_days?: int, session_ids?: list[str]\\nResponse: { \\"deleted_sessions\\": int, \\"deleted_agents\\": int, \\"deleted_messages\\": int }\\n```\\n\\n#### System Stats\\n```\\nGET /api/system/db-stats\\nResponse: { \\"database_size_mb\\": float, \\"table_counts\\": dict, \\"last_vacuum\\": datetime }\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Data Model Changes\\n\\n### Agent Record (swarm_state.py)\\n```python\\n# Existing fields plus:\\nretry_count: int = 0  # Track retry attempts\\ndelete_on_failure: bool = False  # Flag for auto-delete behavior\\n```\\n\\n### New Methods in SwarmState\\n```python\\ndef get_failed_agents(self) -> list[dict]\\ndef increment_retry_count(self, agent_id: str) -> int\\ndef delete_agent(self, agent_id: str, cascade: bool = True) -> bool\\ndef delete_session(self, session_id: str, cascade: bool = True) -> bool\\ndef get_completed_sessions_stats(self) -> dict\\ndef vacuum_database(self) -> bool\\ndef cleanup_orphaned_records(self) -> int\\n```\\n\\n## 6. Data Flow\\n\\n### Retry All Failed Flow\\n```\\nUser clicks \\"Retry All Failed\\" \\n  \\u2192 POST /api/agents/retry-all-failed\\n  \\u2192 SwarmState.get_failed_agents()\\n  \\u2192 For each agent: \\n      set delete_on_failure=True\\n      increment retry_count\\n      queue for recovery\\n  \\u2192 Return count\\n  \\nWhen agent completes recovery:\\n  \\u2192 If failed AND delete_on_failure AND retry_count >= 2:\\n      \\u2192 SwarmState.delete_agent()\\n  \\u2192 Else if succeeded:\\n      \\u2192 Clear retry flags\\n```\\n\\n### Job Cleanup Flow\\n```\\nUser opens JobCleanupPanel\\n  \\u2192 GET /api/jobs/completed/stats\\n  \\u2192 Display completed jobs by age\\n\\nUser selects \\"Delete jobs older than X days\\"\\n  \\u2192 Confirmation modal\\n  \\u2192 DELETE /api/jobs/completed?older_than_days=X\\n  \\u2192 SwarmState.delete_session() for each\\n  \\u2192 SwarmState.vacuum_database()\\n  \\u2192 Return deletion counts\\n  \\u2192 Update UI\\n```\\n\\n## 7. Error Handling\\n\\n### Backend\\n- All delete operations wrapped in transactions\\n- Cascading deletes handled at database level\\n- Return partial success if some deletions fail\\n- Log all deletion operations for audit\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Confirmation modals for destructive actions\\n- Loading states during operations\\n- Error messages for failed operations\\n- Refresh data after successful operations\\n\\n## 8. Performance Considerations\\n\\n### Database Optimizations\\n1. **VACUUM after bulk deletes** - Reclaim space immediately\\n2. **Batch operations** - Delete in chunks of 100 to avoid long locks\\n3. **Index usage** - Ensure indexes on status, session_id, created_at\\n\\n### UI Optimizations\\n1. **Pagination** - Limit initial job list load\\n2. **Debounced updates** - Don\'t refresh on every operation\\n3. **Optimistic updates** - Show immediate UI changes\\n\\n## 9. Security Considerations\\n\\n- All delete endpoints require confirmation\\n- No undo capability (as per requirements)\\n- Log all destructive operations\\n- Consider rate limiting on bulk operations\\n\\n## 10. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Backend Tests\\n- Unit tests for new SwarmState methods\\n- Integration tests for API endpoints\\n- Edge cases: empty databases, partial failures\\n\\n### Frontend Tests\\n- Component tests for JobCleanupPanel\\n- Integration tests for API calls\\n- Modal interaction tests\\n\\n## 11. Migration/Rollback\\n\\n### Database Changes\\n- Add retry_count column (default 0)\\n- Add delete_on_failure column (default false)\\n- Both additive, no breaking changes\\n\\n### Rollback Plan\\n- New columns can remain unused\\n- API endpoints can be disabled via config\\n- Frontend components can be hidden via feature flag\\n\\n## 12. Implementation Checklist\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Backend\\n- [ ] Modify swarm_state.py with new methods\\n- [ ] Modify swarm_recovery.py with retry tracking\\n- [ ] Add API endpoints to main.py\\n- [ ] Write unit tests\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Frontend\\n- [ ] Create JobCleanupPanel component\\n- [ ] Modify RecoveryDashboard\\n- [ ] Update App.jsx routing\\n- [ ] Add confirmation modals\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Performance\\n- [ ] Add VACUUM functionality\\n- [ ] Add db-stats endpoint\\n- [ ] Implement orphan cleanup\\n- [ ] Performance testing\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Dt8vP1trxLoudCq27i4H7c', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Agent Management & Cleanup System - Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nThe user needs to manage failed agents more effectively and clean up old data to improve system performance. Specifically:\\n1. Retry failed agents automatically, and if they fail again, delete them permanently\\n2. Provide a way to delete old completed jobs\\n3. Address system slowness caused by data accumulation\\n\\n## Current State Analysis\\nThe existing system has:\\n- **Recovery system** (`swarm_recovery.py`): Handles agent recovery with multiple strategies (RETRY, ESCALATE_MODEL, ABORT, etc.)\\n- **Swarm state** (`swarm_state.py`): SQLite-backed state management with cleanup_old_data() method\\n- **Backend APIs** (`main.py`): Endpoints for recovery, cleanup, and retention management\\n- **Data retention** (`data_retention.py`): Existing retention management\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Objective 1: Retry Failed Agents with Auto-Delete on Second Failure\\n**Priority: HIGH**\\n\\nCreate a \\"retry and delete\\" feature that:\\n1. Allows user to retry all currently failed agents\\n2. Tracks retry attempts for each failed agent\\n3. Automatically deletes agents that fail a second time after retry\\n4. Shows clear status in the UI of what happened (retried, deleted, succeeded)\\n\\n**Technical Requirements:**\\n- Add new API endpoint: `POST /api/agents/retry-all-failed`\\n  - Finds all agents with status = \'failed\' \\n  - Queues each for retry with a \\"delete_on_failure\\" flag\\n  - Returns count of agents queued for retry\\n- Add new API endpoint: `POST /api/agents/{agent_id}/retry-and-delete`\\n  - Retries single agent, deletes if it fails again\\n- Modify recovery system to track \\"second_failure\\" and auto-delete\\n- Add frontend button \\"Retry All Failed (auto-delete on 2nd failure)\\"\\n\\n### Objective 2: Delete Old Completed Jobs\\n**Priority: HIGH**\\n\\nCreate a job cleanup feature that:\\n1. Shows list of old completed jobs/sessions\\n2. Allows bulk deletion by age (e.g., \\"Delete jobs older than 7 days\\")\\n3. Allows individual deletion of specific completed jobs\\n4. Includes confirmation before destructive actions\\n\\n**Technical Requirements:**\\n- Add new API endpoint: `DELETE /api/jobs/completed`\\n  - Query params: `older_than_days` (optional), `session_ids` (optional list)\\n  - Deletes sessions and all associated data (agents, messages, events, etc.)\\n  - Returns count of deleted items\\n- Add new API endpoint: `GET /api/jobs/completed/stats`\\n  - Returns count and size of completed jobs, grouped by age\\n- Add frontend component for job cleanup:\\n  - Shows completed jobs with age\\n  - Bulk delete by age slider/dropdown\\n  - Individual delete buttons\\n  - Confirmation modal before delete\\n\\n### Objective 3: Performance Improvements\\n**Priority: MEDIUM**\\n\\nAddress system slowness by:\\n1. Adding database vacuuming after bulk deletes\\n2. Implementing smarter data loading (pagination, lazy loading)\\n3. Adding database size monitoring\\n4. Cleaning up orphaned data\\n\\n**Technical Requirements:**\\n- Add `VACUUM` after bulk deletes\\n- Add API to get database size: `GET /api/system/db-stats`\\n- Add cleanup of orphaned records (messages/events without parent agents)\\n- Consider adding index optimizations if needed\\n\\n## Scope Constraints\\n**IN SCOPE:**\\n- Backend API endpoints for the features above\\n- Frontend UI components for retry and cleanup\\n- Modifications to existing recovery system\\n- Documentation updates\\n\\n**OUT OF SCOPE:**\\n- Automatic scheduled cleanup (can be added later)\\n- Archive to external storage (just delete for now)\\n- Undo/recovery of deleted data\\n- Complex data migration\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. User can click one button to retry all failed agents\\n2. Agents that fail twice are automatically deleted\\n3. User can see and delete old completed jobs by age\\n4. System performance noticeably improves after cleanup\\n5. All existing functionality continues to work\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must work with existing SQLite database schema\\n- Must not break existing API endpoints\\n- Must be accessible from the existing React frontend\\n- Should follow existing code patterns\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- \\"Failed agents\\" means agents with status = \'failed\' in the database\\n- \\"Completed jobs\\" means sessions with status = \'completed\'\\n- \\"Delete\\" means permanent removal from database (no soft delete)\\n- Performance issues are primarily from data volume, not code issues\\n\\n## Files to Modify/Create\\n\\n### Backend (Python)\\n1. **src/runtime/agents/swarm_recovery.py** - Add retry-and-delete logic\\n2. **src/runtime/agents/swarm_state.py** - Add delete methods\\n3. **src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py** - Add new API endpoints\\n\\n### Frontend (React)\\n1. **New: src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/JobCleanupPanel.jsx** - UI for job cleanup\\n2. **Modify: RecoveryDashboard.jsx** - Add retry-all-failed button\\n3. **Modify: App.jsx** - Add navigation to cleanup panel\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n1. First: API endpoints for retry-all-failed and delete completed jobs\\n2. Second: Modify recovery system for auto-delete on second failure\\n3. Third: Frontend components\\n4. Fourth: Performance optimizations and testing\\n"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 92.1%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.9\n- Common errors to avoid: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
