tent': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018L1tf8f7dRxoZmzNaeurqM', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Agent Management & Cleanup System'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_018L1tf8f7dRxoZmzNaeurqM', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LwPMTpXNYfJgebKyDfiFg7', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LwPMTpXNYfJgebKyDfiFg7', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: API Cost Optimization System\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Design Philosophy\\nA flexible, extensible multi-provider architecture that enables intelligent, cost-effective AI model routing while maintaining system reliability and output quality.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n- **Layered Architecture** with clear separation of concerns\\n- **Strategy Pattern** for provider management\\n- **Decorator/Proxy Pattern** for quality monitoring and fallback\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Provider SDKs**: \\n  - Anthropic Claude: `anthropic` \\n  - OpenAI: `openai`\\n  - Local Providers: Custom REST client\\n\\n### Key Libraries\\n- `pydantic` for configuration and validation\\n- `asyncio` for concurrent provider interactions\\n- `prometheus_client` for metrics tracking\\n- `structlog` for structured logging\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### A. Provider Management Layer\\n```\\nProviderManager\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 BaseProvider (Abstract Base Class)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AnthropicProvider\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 OpenAIProvider\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 LocalClaudeProvider\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ProviderRegistry\\n```\\n\\n#### Responsibilities:\\n- Standardized interface for different AI providers\\n- Dynamic provider registration\\n- Health check mechanisms\\n- Credential management\\n\\n### B. Smart Router\\n```\\nSmartRouter\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TaskAnalyzer\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AutonomyClassifier\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProviderSelector\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 CostOptimizer\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 QualityPredictor\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 FallbackHandler\\n```\\n\\n#### Responsibilities:\\n- Analyze task complexity and autonomy\\n- Select most appropriate provider\\n- Implement intelligent fallback logic\\n\\n### C. Quality Monitoring\\n```\\nQualityMonitor\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 OutputValidator\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ModelQualityScorer\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 CostTracker\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 PerformanceReporter\\n```\\n\\n#### Responsibilities:\\n- Validate model output quality\\n- Track per-provider performance\\n- Generate cost optimization reports\\n\\n## 4. File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 providers/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 base_provider.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 anthropic_provider.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 openai_provider.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 local_claude_provider.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 routing/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 smart_router.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 task_analyzer.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 provider_selector.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 monitoring/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 quality_monitor.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 output_validator.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 cost_tracker.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 config/\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 providers.yaml\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 cost_rules.json\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Data Flow\\n\\n```\\nTask Submission \\n  \\u2193\\nTaskAnalyzer (Complexity & Autonomy Assessment)\\n  \\u2193\\nProviderSelector (Select Optimal Provider)\\n  \\u2193\\nSelected Provider Execution\\n  \\u2193\\nQualityMonitor (Validate Output)\\n  \\u2193\\nResult Return or Fallback\\n```\\n\\n## 6. Configuration Management\\n\\n### Provider Configuration (providers.yaml)\\n```yaml\\nproviders:\\n  anthropic:\\n    default_model: claude-2\\n    priority: 1\\n  openai:\\n    default_model: gpt-4\\n    priority: 2\\n  local_claude:\\n    endpoint: http://localhost:8000\\n    priority: 3\\n```\\n\\n## 7. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Containerization\\n- Docker containers for each provider adapter\\n- Kubernetes for orchestration and scaling\\n- Helm charts for configuration management\\n\\n### CI/CD\\n- GitHub Actions for testing\\n- Automated provider health checks\\n- Feature flag support for gradual rollout\\n\\n## 8. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Test Suites\\n- Unit Tests: Provider adapters, routing logic\\n- Integration Tests: Cross-provider workflows\\n- Performance Tests: Provider latency and cost\\n- Chaos Tests: Simulate provider failures\\n\\n### Quality Metrics\\n- Output similarity across providers\\n- Latency comparisons\\n- Cost per successful task\\n- Fallback success rates\\n\\n## 9. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. Inconsistent model quality\\n2. Higher complexity\\n3. Performance overhead\\n\\n### Mitigation Strategies\\n- Comprehensive quality scoring\\n- Intelligent caching\\n- Minimal abstraction overhead\\n- Detailed performance monitoring\\n\\n## 10. Open Questions for User\\n\\n1. Specific OpenAI model preferences?\\n2. Tolerance for minor quality variations?\\n3. Acceptable fallback chain priorities?\\n\\n## 11. Future Extensibility\\n\\n- Easy addition of new providers\\n- Pluggable quality assessment algorithms\\n- Machine learning-based provider selection\\n\\n## Appendix: Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Research & Base Infrastructure\\n- Provider abstract interfaces\\n- Basic routing mechanisms\\n- Logging and metrics setup\\n\\n### Phase 2: OpenAI Integration\\n- OpenAI provider implementation\\n- Cost tracking enhancements\\n- Initial routing logic\\n\\n### Phase 3: Local Claude Support\\n- Local provider detection\\n- Health check mechanisms\\n- Fallback implementations\\n\\n## Performance Targets\\n\\n- Reduce API costs by 40%\\n- Maintain 95% output quality\\n- < 50ms additional routing overhead"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PXKnu8NwKYojWEqLaTXAZd', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Architecture: Agent Management & Cleanup System\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n### Design Philosophy\nExtend the existing ensemble UI system with retry-and-delete functionality for failed agents, job cleanup features, and performance optimizations while maintaining backwards compatibility.\n\n### Architecture Pattern\n- **Extension Architecture** - Adding to existing FastAPI backend and React frontend\n- **Repository Pattern** - Using existing `SwarmState` for data operations\n- **Service Pattern** - New service layer for retry and cleanup logic\n\n## 2. Tech Stack (Existing)\n\n### Backend\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\n- **Database**: SQLite via SwarmState\n- **Recovery**: swarm_recovery.py (existing)\n- **State Management**: swarm_state.py (existing)\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React\n- **Components**: Existing RecoveryDashboard, App.jsx\n- **Styling**: Existing CSS/component library\n\n## 3. System Components\n\n### A. Backend - New/Modified Components\n\n```\nsrc/runtime/agents/\n├── swarm_recovery.py (MODIFY)\n│   └── Add: track retry attempts, auto-delete on second failure\n├── swarm_state.py (MODIFY)\n│   └── Add: delete_agent(), delete_session(), get_completed_sessions_stats()\n│\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/backend/\n└── main.py (MODIFY)\n    └── Add: retry-all-failed, retry-and-delete, job cleanup endpoints\n```\n\n### B. Frontend - New/Modified Components\n\n```\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\n├── components/\n│   ├── JobCleanupPanel.jsx (NEW)\n│   │   ├── CompletedJobsList\n│   │   ├── AgeFilterSelector\n│   │   ├── BulkDeleteButton\n│   │   └── ConfirmationModal\n│   └── RecoveryDashboard.jsx (MODIFY)\n│       └── Add: RetryAllFailedButton\n├── App.jsx (MODIFY)\n│   └── Add: Route to JobCleanupPanel\n```\n\n## 4. API Design\n\n### New Endpoints\n\n#### Retry Failed Agents\n```\nPOST /api/agents/retry-all-failed\nResponse: { "queued_count": int, "agent_ids": list[str] }\n\nPOST /api/agents/{agent_id}/retry-and-delete\nResponse: { "status": "queued" | "deleted" | "succeeded", "agent_id": str }\n```\n\n#### Job Cleanup\n```\nGET /api/jobs/completed/stats\nResponse: {\n  "total_completed": int,\n  "by_age": [\n    { "age_days": "0-7", "count": int, "size_mb": float },\n    { "age_days": "7-30", "count": int, "size_mb": float },\n    { "age_days": "30+", "count": int, "size_mb": float }\n  ]\n}\n\nDELETE /api/jobs/completed\nQuery Params: older_than_days?: int, session_ids?: list[str]\nResponse: { "deleted_sessions": int, "deleted_agents": int, "deleted_messages": int }\n```\n\n#### System Stats\n```\nGET /api/system/db-stats\nResponse: { "database_size_mb": float, "table_counts": dict, "last_vacuum": datetime }\n```\n\n## 5. Data Model Changes\n\n### Agent Record (swarm_state.py)\n```python\n# Existing fields plus:\nretry_count: int = 0  # Track retry attempts\ndelete_on_failure: bool = False  # Flag for auto-delete behavior\n```\n\n### New Methods in SwarmState\n```python\ndef get_failed_agents(self) -> list[dict]\ndef increment_retry_count(self, agent_id: str) -> int\ndef delete_agent(self, agent_id: str, cascade: bool = True) -> bool\ndef delete_session(self, session_id: str, cascade: bool = True) -> bool\ndef get_completed_sessions_stats(self) -> dict\ndef vacuum_database(self) -> bool\ndef cleanup_orphaned_records(self) -> int\n```\n\n## 6. Data Flow\n\n### Retry All Failed Flow\n```\nUser clicks "Retry All Failed" \n  → POST /api/agents/retry-all-failed\n  → SwarmState.get_failed_agents()\n  → For each agent: \n      set delete_on_failure=True\n      increment retry_count\n      queue for recovery\n  → Return count\n  \nWhen agent completes recovery:\n  → If failed AND delete_on_failure AND retry_count >= 2:\n      → SwarmState.delete_agent()\n  → Else if succeeded:\n      → Clear retry flags\n```\n\n### Job Cleanup Flow\n```\nUser opens JobCleanupPanel\n  → GET /api/jobs/completed/stats\n  → Display completed jobs by age\n\nUser selects "Delete jobs older than X days"\n  → Confirmation modal\n  → DELETE /api/jobs/completed?older_than_days=X\n  → SwarmState.delete_session() for each\n  → SwarmState.vacuum_database()\n  → Return deletion counts\n  → Update UI\n```\n\n## 7. Error Handling\n\n### Backend\n- All delete operations wrapped in transactions\n- Cascading deletes handled at database level\n- Return partial success if some deletions fail\n- Log all deletion operations for audit\n\n### Frontend\n- Confirmation modals for destructive actions\n- Loading states during operations\n- Error messages for failed operations\n- Refresh data after successful operations\n\n## 8. Performance Considerations\n\n### Database Optimizations\n1. **VACUUM after bulk deletes** - Reclaim space immediately\n2. **Batch operations** - Delete in chunks of 100 to avoid long locks\n3. **Index usage** - Ensure indexes on status, session_id, created_at\n\n### UI Optimizations\n1. **Pagination** - Limit initial job list load\n2. **Debounced updates** - Don\'t refresh on every operation\n3. **Optimistic updates** - Show immediate UI changes\n\n## 9. Security Considerations\n\n- All delete endpoints require confirmation\n- No undo capability (as per requirements)\n- Log all destructive operations\n- Consider rate limiting on bulk operations\n\n## 10. Testing Strategy\n\n### Backend Tests\n- Unit tests for new SwarmState methods\n- Integration tests for API endpoints\n- Edge cases: empty databases, partial failures\n\n### Frontend Tests\n- Component tests for JobCleanupPanel\n- Integration tests for API calls\n- Modal interaction tests\n\n## 11. Migration/Rollback\n\n### Database Changes\n- Add retry_count column (default 0)\n- Add delete_on_failure column (default false)\n- Both additive, no breaking changes\n\n### Rollback Plan\n- New columns can remain unused\n- API endpoints can be disabled via config\n- Frontend components can be hidden via feature flag\n\n## 12. Implementation Checklist\n\n### Milestone 1: Backend\n- [ ] Modify swarm_state.py with new methods\n- [ ] Modify swarm_recovery.py with retry tracking\n- [ ] Add API endpoints to main.py\n- [ ] Write unit tests\n\n### Milestone 2: Frontend\n- [ ] Create JobCleanupPanel component\n- [ ] Modify RecoveryDashboard\n- [ ] Update App.jsx routing\n- [ ] Add confirmation modals\n\n### Milestone 3: Performance\n- [ ] Add VACUUM functionality\n- [ ] Add db-stats endpoint\n- [ ] Implement orphan cleanup\n- [ ] Performance testing\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PXKnu8NwKYojWEqLaTXAZd', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_232856.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_232856.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01G7ZrNrFzs9q1Ug61KtAhQ8', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '62a796ef', 'note': 'Architecture document created. System Architect returned incorrect architecture (for API Cost Optimization instead of Agent Management). Corrected manually with proper architecture for this project.', 'category': 'decision'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MiBSa6gyW3PvA2kRwLRixq', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'update_task', 'project_id': '62a796ef', 'task_id': '07973fe6', 'status': 'in_progress', 'note': 'Starting Milestone 1 - Backend API Foundation'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01G7ZrNrFzs9q1Ug61KtAhQ8', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MiBSa6gyW3PvA2kRwLRixq', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Updated task status to in_progress"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XfEUP7Ywy18VWrWyY3FJE7', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/backend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Milestone 1: Backend API Foundation - Create retry-failed and job cleanup API endpoints including: POST /api/agents/retry-all-failed, POST /api/agents/{agent_id}/retry-and-delete, DELETE /api/jobs/completed, GET /api/jobs/completed/stats, GET /api/system/db-stats. Modify swarm_recovery.py for retry tracking and auto-delete on second failure. Modify swarm_state.py with new delete methods.', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_t